## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to quantify costs and benefits of a client-side policy engine with offline operation, privacy constraints, and staged rollout.

## Key Concepts

- On-device budgeting and telemetry
- Offline-first synchronization
- Privacy, consent, and compliance
- Rollout strategies and risk controls
- Break-even horizon and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: compute CBA estimate
function computeCBA(inputs){
  const ramMB = inputs.ram || 30;
  const energyPerHour = inputs.energy || 1.0;
  const dataTxKB = inputs.dataTx || 150;
  return { ramMB, energyPerHour, dataTxKB };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the CBA if privacy laws tighten data retention or encryption requirements?
- What telemetry would you deploy to validate drift and performance post-rollout, and how would you act on anomalies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cost-aware, privacy-preserving on-device ML feature with hardware constraints and OTA workflows.

## Key Concepts
- On-device graph neural networks
- Privacy-preserving data handling
- OTA delta updates
- Drift detection and validation
- ECU hardware constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code snippet for delta update application
function applyDelta(model, delta) {
  // merge weights with low-precision quantization
  for (let i=0; i<model.length; i++) model[i] = saturate(model[i] + delta[i], -128, 127);
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy and security in OTA payload?
- How to handle drift when sensors drop or fail to report?
